Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:09:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/24] Modeling Algorithms - Fix the fillet corner patch at
 the vertex of a sharp edge

PerformMoreThreeCorner limits the sharp edges at the corner by a new point
where the patch meets them. When the patch meets an edge exactly at the
corner vertex, the edge is cut at its own end. If the other end of the same
edge is cut by another patch (fillets along both ends of a quarter turn of
a square on a box, FreeCAD issue 27807), the rebuilt edge keeps its old
vertex at one end and the face wire is not closed. In this case the edge
is kept whole and the patch ends at the corner vertex itself, as is done
already when two fillets meet at the corner.

The patch is a plate with tangency (G1) constraints along the fillets.
When the fillets meet the faces at the corner at angles that no smooth
patch can follow, the plate misses the tangency by far anyway (1.2 to 1.5
rad on the test parts of FreeCAD issues 27807, 31894 and 20085), and the
constraints only make it wave: it bulged out of the shape by up to 3.5 mm
on fillets of 0.5 mm and left gaps of 0.1 to 0.6 mm along its boundary.
If the tangency error of the plate exceeds 0.5 rad, it is built again
through the curves alone and kept if it is at least as close to them and
can be approximated; the edges between the patch and the fillets are then
not marked as smooth. Otherwise the first plate is used as before. The
constraints are kept in the order they were added, since GeomPlate
reorders its own list.

